.SH NAME
ns_register_cgi \- Register CGI handlers
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBns_register_cgi\fR ?\fB-constraints \fIconstraints\fR\fR? ?\fB-noinherit\fR? ?\fB-matchsegments\fR? ?\fB-path \fIvalue\fR\fR? ?--? \fImethod\fR \fIurl\fR
.sp
.BE
.SH DESCRIPTION
This document describes how to register a CGI handler programmatically\&.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBns_register_cgi\fR ?\fB-constraints \fIconstraints\fR\fR? ?\fB-noinherit\fR? ?\fB-matchsegments\fR? ?\fB-path \fIvalue\fR\fR? ?--? \fImethod\fR \fIurl\fR
The command registers the CGI handler for requests matching \fImethod\fR and
\fIURL\fR to be handled as CGI programs\&. The specified \fIurl\fR can
contain a match pattern, which is handled by the NaviServer urlspace
(like in \fBns_register_proc\fR)\&. The match will always be a match on
the last URL segment, unless \fB-matchsegments\fR is specified\&.
.sp
The option \fB-constraints\fR allows you to specify
additional context constraints to specify, when this handler should
be invoked (for details see
\fIContext Constraints\fR [\&.\&./\&.\&./manual/files/ns_urlspace\&.html#section5])\&.
.sp
If \fB-noinherit\fR is specified, the request URL must match
the directory of the registered URL\&.
.sp
If \fB-matchsegments\fR is specified, the pattern will be
matched with all segments of the request URL\&.
.sp
The \fB-path\fR specifies the source location for the files
in case the request URL matches the register URL\&. The provided source
location is registered via \fBns_register_fasturl2file\fR such that
\fBfastpath\fR can resolve the request path against this source
location\&.
.sp
Handlers registered with \fBns_register_cgi\fR can be
unregistered via \fBns_unregister_op\fR\&. In case the \fB-path\fR
was specified, it can be unregistered with
\fBns_unregister_url2file\fR\&.
.sp
The mapping via \fBns_register_cgi\fR is the programmatical
counterpart to define the mapping via the configuration file in the
section "ns/server/$servername/module/nscgi" (see \fBnscgi\fR)\&.
.PP
.SH EXAMPLE
.CS


 # Bind CGI handler for /admin/panel only when the incoming request
 # has the specified request header field\&.
 ns_register_cgi -constraints {X-User *admin*} GET /admin/Panel \&.\&.\&.

.CE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
ns_register, nscgi
.SH KEYWORDS
CGI, callback, context constraints, fastpath, handler, nscgi, request, urlspace
